From 2c8de9c7ec4d5cd52942e8b990d608b0f7d6b51c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yashgix <125082291+yashgix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:05:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Report unsendable OpenAPI operations during import

An operation is left out with its reason when its path has a placeholder with no declared path parameter, writes a declared parameter as :name, *name or beside a regex group such as (\d+), has a stray brace such as /users/{id?}, or is a GET or HEAD that requires a body. An optional GET or HEAD body, and a declared path parameter the path does not hold, are not sent and are named in the tool description, so the tool stays callable.

Release-note: Fix: OpenAPI imports now explain which operations cannot be called and why, instead of offering tools that always fail.
